T:Original greeting-and-freeze dance game
C:Grand Central Stationery (AI-assisted original, CC0)
O:Course original (no cultural attribution)
R:early-years dance-pop listening bridge
S:Grand Central Stationery, CBC Modern Canadian Bridges (original course composition, 11 November 2026), CC0 1.0
N:Original SK dance-pop listening bridge and accessible movement game; the class sings two repeated greetings, follows one selected movement, then chooses the size and energy of the ending.
N:Listen: Jeremy and Jazzy — "Funky Freeze Dance" (2022), from Say Hello, on CBC Kids, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vmx4lS7xUsM. Notice the reliable dance pulse, a short memorable vocal hook and the way production drops or adds layers to frame a choice to move.
N:Jeremy and Jazzy is a CBC Kids series whose songs are by Juno-nominated Canadian songwriter Jeremy Fisher, with Aiza Ntibarikure as Jazzy; Say Hello was nominated for the 2023 Juno for Children's Album. It replaces the first choice, Carly Rae Jepsen's "Don't Leave Me on the Dance Floor", whose words do not suit SK.
N:Original C-major pentatonic tune and words; nothing from "Funky Freeze Dance" is used, and the freeze is a classroom game, not its choreography.
N:Published early: an AI-assisted original written for this course and released CC0, not traditional and not by any artist named above. Not yet tried with a class or read by its reviewers (SK classroom teacher, movement/accessibility reviewer, second score reader and student listening trial); its workshop record is kept for correction.
