R:Grade 1 country-pop listening bridge
S:Grand Central Stationery, CBC Modern Canadian Bridges (original course composition, 11 November 2026), CC0 1.0
N:Original Grade 1 country-pop listening bridge; a caller sings the first two bars, the class answers, and a student selects an accented, detached or smooth body-percussion reply.
N:Listen: Shania Twain — "Up!" (2002), the green country version, official video; on CBC Music's 2021 Music Class Challenge list, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-FMhUNSIxks. Listen for how a country-pop song combines a direct story, a firm backbeat, short hooks and contrasting vocal articulation.
N:Shania Twain grew up in Timmins, Ontario, and is the best-selling woman in country music history. "Up!" turns a bad day around ("can only go up from here"); its country mix is the one to play, not the red pop mix. It replaces the first choice, "Faded Blue Jeans" (2026), whose words do not suit Grade 1.
N:Original three-note E-G-A classroom tune and words; no hook, words, chords, fiddle or drum part from "Up!" is used.
N:Published early: an AI-assisted original written for this course and released CC0, not traditional and not by any artist named above. Not yet tried with a class or read by its reviewers (Grade 1 music teacher, accessibility reviewer, second score reader and student singing trial); its workshop record is kept for correction.
