N:Original Grade 2 indie-folk listening bridge; students sing an AB travel song over a do-so bordun, vary one two-bar window, then choose the dynamic shape of the arrival.
N:Listen: Braden Lam — "Coquihalla" (2026), official video; its words are not yet checked, so preview it, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eGfUKN0hEzQ. Hear how indie folk-pop can turn travel and place into an intimate story through acoustic colour, a repeated pulse and a widening chorus.
N:Braden Lam is a Canadian indie-folk songwriter based in Halifax; the referenced release takes its title from British Columbia's Coquihalla route.
N:Original pentatonic tune, fictional window lyric and C-G bordun; no lyric, melodic phrase, guitar figure or chord progression from "Coquihalla" is used.
