R:Grade 4 Francophone electro-pop listening bridge
S:Grand Central Stationery, CBC Modern Canadian Bridges (original course composition, 11 November 2026), CC0 1.0
N:Original Grade 4 Francophone electro/dream-pop listening bridge; students sing a syncopated ABBA song, compare parallel major and minor colour, and select the final texture in real time.
N:Listen: Claudia Bouvette — "Amour écran" (Bonsound, 2026), official visualizer; a love song, so preview it, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N6lD52RQbJI. Hear how airy synthesizer timbres, an insistent electronic pulse and an 1980s-coloured major/minor haze can support intimate French-language pop writing.
N:Claudia Bouvette is a Montréal singer-songwriter; she wrote "Amour écran" with her creative partner Soran, and Bonsound released it in August 2026.
N:Original French words, melody and C major/C minor contrast; no words, melodic cell, synth sound, bass line or chord progression from "Amour écran" is used.
N:Published early: an AI-assisted original written for this course and released CC0, not traditional and not by any artist named above. Not yet tried with a class or read by its reviewers (Grade 4 teacher, Francophone language reviewer, Francophone Canadian music educator, second score reader and student trial); its workshop record is kept for correction. The French words were rewritten on 12 November 2026 to fit the notes (one syllable to a note, sung mute e's counted) and want a Francophone reader.
