N:Original Grade 8 orchestral/collective indie-rock arranging bridge; students distribute melody, chords, pedal and counterline across available voices and instruments, then justify a live texture plan for the final four bars.
N:Listen: Broken Social Scene — "Anthems for a Seventeen Year-Old Girl", from You Forgot It in People (2002), official video, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wLaDksDOcE4. Hear how a Canadian indie-rock collective builds emotional scale through repetition, accumulating instruments, changing timbres and multiple musicians sharing an arrangement.
N:Broken Social Scene is a Toronto musical collective. The reference credits multiple writers and its arrangement is known for a repeated vocal idea surrounded by gradually expanding banjo, strings and band texture.
N:Original D-mixolydian melody, lyric, counterline, metre changes and D-C-G harmony; no words, melody, banjo figure, string line, form or production detail from the reference is used.
